WEBVTT

00:00:00.820 --> 00:00:01.500
Welcome.

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:04.900
This course develops business judgment for AI adoption.

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:09.900
AWS emphasizes taking AI from adoption to scale.

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:15.070
The focus is evaluating AI investments,

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:19.610
building business cases, designing governance, and scaling adoption.

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:26.150
The goal is to connect AI decisions to measurable outcomes, across organizations and

00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:26.490
industries.

00:00:29.660 --> 00:00:30.400
Why learn it?

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:36.580
These skills help you decide where AI fits, justify investment, manage risk, and expand

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:37.260
what works.

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:42.060
We will practice that reasoning, rather than promise a particular career outcome.

00:00:46.363 --> 00:00:52.123
This is for people who lead or influence AI outcomes: product and program managers,

00:00:52.663 --> 00:00:54.903
business leaders, analysts, consultants,

00:00:55.523 --> 00:00:57.083
and marketing or sales professionals.

00:00:58.023 --> 00:00:59.723
You do not have to build the models yourself.

00:01:03.933 --> 00:01:09.413
AWS recommends basic AI familiarity and six months alongside AI initiatives.

00:01:10.353 --> 00:01:12.213
Coding, implementation experience,

00:01:12.953 --> 00:01:14.913
and another certification are not required.

00:01:14.913 --> 00:01:16.033
AI

00:01:18.173 --> 00:01:24.893
Practitioner validates foundational AI concepts and AWS AI service knowledge.

00:01:25.413 --> 00:01:30.633
Business Strategist focuses on choosing investments, building business cases, managing

00:01:30.633 --> 00:01:32.133
risk, and driving adoption.

00:01:33.173 --> 00:01:34.213
Earning both is optional.
